WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.544
[♪ upbeat music plays]

00:30.322 --> 00:33.951
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

00:44.044 --> 00:46.755
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION - SOME
SCENES WERE GENERATED USING AI

00:46.838 --> 00:48.966
CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
WERE FILMED SAFELY

00:49.049 --> 00:51.051
[♪ gentle music plays]

00:53.011 --> 00:54.012
Hwayeong.

01:22.583 --> 01:26.628
[♪ tense music plays]

01:34.636 --> 01:37.264
[♪ melancholy ballad plays]

01:52.487 --> 01:54.614
[song continues]

02:15.427 --> 02:17.721
[music distorts, stutters]

02:19.681 --> 02:21.433
-[device beeps]
-[automated voice, in English] Power off.

02:21.516 --> 02:23.060
[in Korean] Just listen to it.

02:25.771 --> 02:28.190
Come on, just try listening to it for now.

02:28.273 --> 02:30.359
Music is good for treating anxiety.

02:31.318 --> 02:32.653
It's out of battery.

02:32.736 --> 02:34.279
Huh?

02:34.905 --> 02:38.116
I charged it yesterday, though.
Give me a second.

02:38.200 --> 02:40.661
-I should have a power bank.
-[announcer] …is now departing.

02:41.244 --> 02:42.663
Do you want to chew on this?

02:44.164 --> 02:47.250
Chewing on something can help you relax.

02:50.754 --> 02:52.506
I told you I'm okay.

02:53.590 --> 02:55.550
You're not okay, though.

02:56.385 --> 02:58.637
You were crying yesterday.

02:58.720 --> 03:01.765
Excuse me, please wake up.

03:01.848 --> 03:03.225
Seonu…

03:03.308 --> 03:04.309
Sorry?

03:06.895 --> 03:07.896
Seonu…

03:09.272 --> 03:10.524
You were saying "Seonu."

03:11.274 --> 03:13.568
[♪ somber music plays]

03:19.616 --> 03:20.826
Do you know me?

03:21.618 --> 03:22.828
Sorry?

03:22.911 --> 03:24.579
Did I ever ask for your help?

03:26.331 --> 03:27.332
Ah…

03:27.916 --> 03:30.001
Well, no, but I--

03:30.085 --> 03:33.004
I'm sorry you had to help me
like that yesterday, but…

03:34.423 --> 03:35.841
I never asked for your help.

03:37.300 --> 03:40.095
So just be on your way
and stop crossing the line.

03:40.971 --> 03:42.347
[stammers] What?
STYLE
::cue()

03:46.601 --> 03:49.604
Wait, when did I ever cross the…

03:49.688 --> 03:50.897
[ship horn blowing]

03:50.981 --> 03:52.566
Excuse me!

03:58.280 --> 03:59.489
[sighs]

04:01.241 --> 04:02.367
What the hell? Sheesh.

04:03.743 --> 04:08.123
Hey, I need to get on a ferry right away,
so I'm going to need a prescription.

04:08.206 --> 04:09.916
-[horn honks]
-I'll head to your hospital.

04:10.000 --> 04:11.668
I'm heading over right now.

04:13.295 --> 04:14.379
[ship horn blowing]

04:14.463 --> 04:15.881
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

04:15.964 --> 04:18.008
[Ms. Hwang] The last ferry came
and went ages ago.

04:18.091 --> 04:20.260
How come Dr. Do Jiui still isn't here?

04:20.343 --> 04:24.306
I know. He couldn't have deserted his post
on his first day, right?

04:24.389 --> 04:26.516
-Sheesh.
-By the way, Ms. Hwang,

04:26.600 --> 04:28.602
a newbie is joining us next week, right?

04:28.685 --> 04:31.980
I'm going to be really nice to her.

04:32.063 --> 04:33.273
Newbie?

04:34.149 --> 04:38.111
You said the new nurse
is in her third year. I'm in my fourth.

04:38.195 --> 04:40.197
Doesn't that make her the newbie?

04:40.280 --> 04:42.657
[chuckles] I guess you're right,

04:42.741 --> 04:45.368
but she won't be your typical newbie,
just so you know.

04:45.452 --> 04:47.537
She hasn't even been a nurse
for that long,

04:47.621 --> 04:49.414
so imagine how awkward she'll feel.

04:49.498 --> 04:51.291
I should help her out.

04:51.374 --> 04:54.503
I've even organized
all the handover notes.

04:54.586 --> 04:57.923
-Oh, okay. Well done.
-[chuckles]

04:58.757 --> 05:01.968
As to who will end up helping whom,
we won't know until she gets here,

05:02.052 --> 05:03.637
but well done.

05:03.720 --> 05:05.514
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

05:05.597 --> 05:06.973
[grunts] Dr. Do.

05:07.057 --> 05:08.725
Hmm, what?

05:08.809 --> 05:12.813
Goodness, Dr. Do!
Do you have any idea what time…

05:12.896 --> 05:17.359
My gosh. You look like death.
What happened to you?

05:17.442 --> 05:20.445
I'm sorry. I fell asleep on the ferry.

05:21.363 --> 05:24.032
So you were sleeping on the ferry
all this time?

05:25.367 --> 05:26.368
Yes.

05:26.451 --> 05:29.579
[scoffs] Must be nice being
that unbothered.

05:29.663 --> 05:32.082
Sleeping fine while ditching work.

05:42.676 --> 05:45.011
-[♪ gentle music plays]
-[Hari] Do you want to chew on this?

05:45.595 --> 05:48.473
Chewing on something can help you relax.

05:48.974 --> 05:51.017
FEELING DOWN?
HERE'S A PICK-ME-UP!

05:55.230 --> 05:56.439
[sighs]

06:07.701 --> 06:13.498
EPISODE 2
THE WOMAN WHO CROSSES THE LINE

06:13.582 --> 06:14.791
[music ends]

06:16.543 --> 06:18.712
-[Jiui] Bellflower roots?
-That's right.

06:18.795 --> 06:22.007
-They're precious wild bellflower roots.
-Mmm.

06:22.090 --> 06:25.010
So, about that…
You saved the chief's life last week,

06:25.093 --> 06:28.263
so the youth association
told me to give it to you.

06:29.055 --> 06:31.349
It's from the youth association?
Thank you.

06:31.433 --> 06:32.809
[coughing]

06:35.604 --> 06:38.607
By the way, Mr. Lee Jangsu,
what brings you in today?

06:38.690 --> 06:42.527
I'm just here
to get those meds I always take.

06:42.611 --> 06:44.821
Those meds you always take? [sighs]

06:44.905 --> 06:47.657
[coughing]

06:47.741 --> 06:50.243
You already took
two weeks' worth a week ago.

06:50.327 --> 06:53.580
Two weeks' worth
will barely cut it anymore.

06:53.663 --> 06:56.666
My wife also takes it and all,

06:56.750 --> 07:00.545
so give us about
a month's worth this time.

07:01.129 --> 07:03.965
Did you just say you share your meds
with your wife?

07:04.049 --> 07:05.675
Yes.

07:05.759 --> 07:07.677
No. Proxy prescriptions are illegal.

07:07.761 --> 07:10.138
Strictly speaking,
it's not a proxy prescription,

07:10.221 --> 07:12.682
since I'm also taking those meds.

07:12.766 --> 07:13.767
I still can't do it.

07:13.850 --> 07:17.437
And the coughing might turn into pneumonia
if it continues for two weeks or more,

07:17.520 --> 07:19.064
so I'll give you three days' worth.

07:19.147 --> 07:20.857
Come back after finishing it.

07:20.940 --> 07:22.942
I'm busy as hell because of the anchovies!

07:23.026 --> 07:25.278
And you expect me to visit regularly?

07:25.904 --> 07:28.573
That's the only way I can properly
assess your condition, sir.

07:28.657 --> 07:31.826
I know my condition best.
STYLE
::cue()

07:31.910 --> 07:33.536
I'll take care of myself,

07:33.620 --> 07:35.205
so just give me 30 days' worth.

07:36.498 --> 07:38.500
-I can't do that.
-That's how it's always been!

07:38.583 --> 07:40.418
You're just going to cut me off like this?

07:40.502 --> 07:42.879
[Ms. Hwang] Cough medicine,
something for your phlegm,

07:42.962 --> 07:45.965
antibiotics, and this long one is
the stomach coating agent.

07:46.049 --> 07:49.552
Take one packet in the morning
and in the evening after a meal.

07:49.636 --> 07:53.098
[grunts] Did you really
only put three days' worth in there?

07:53.932 --> 07:54.933
[chuckles]

07:55.016 --> 07:58.520
We only put in
as much as the doctor prescribed.

07:58.603 --> 08:00.939
That's the law.

08:01.022 --> 08:04.859
Is there a law saying
civil servants can ignore residents?

08:04.943 --> 08:07.278
Who said anything about ignoring anyone?

08:07.362 --> 08:10.615
That's not it. It's just how the law is.

08:10.699 --> 08:12.325
Hey, you think I don't know the law?

08:12.409 --> 08:14.035
Law this, law that!

08:14.619 --> 08:18.289
Looks like I'll have to take legal action
against you civil servants

08:18.373 --> 08:20.375
who love the law so much
as a wake-up call!

08:20.458 --> 08:21.543
Wait!

08:21.626 --> 08:24.879
Have you been drinking?
Calm down a little, so I can explain…

08:32.512 --> 08:34.222
-What should we do?
-Sorry?

08:34.806 --> 08:38.476
Word is Mr. Lee actually went to
the county office to file a complaint.

08:38.560 --> 08:39.686
Ah.

08:39.769 --> 08:42.397
[nurse] Looks like things will get
quite troublesome for a while.

08:46.192 --> 08:49.195
Doc, loosen up a little, will you?

08:49.863 --> 08:53.825
Duking it out with the residents
is never easy.

08:54.409 --> 08:56.036
It can't be helped.

08:56.119 --> 08:58.455
-Thank you for the meal.
-Thank you.

08:59.330 --> 09:01.082
Which brings us to my point.

09:01.666 --> 09:05.170
If it won't be a big issue,
how about we just do as they ask?

09:05.253 --> 09:06.921
That's better for everyone, no?

09:07.005 --> 09:10.467
Giving patients
whatever prescriptions they ask for

09:10.550 --> 09:12.427
isn't necessarily "better for everyone."

09:12.510 --> 09:14.512
Nothing good comes
from giving in to patients.

09:17.724 --> 09:19.684
I'm not saying this for my own good, okay?

09:19.768 --> 09:21.519
It's because I'm worried about you guys.

09:21.603 --> 09:23.271
If you keep doing as you please,

09:23.354 --> 09:25.565
something terrible is
going to happen to you!

09:26.107 --> 09:27.692
You'll see once it happens to you.

09:27.776 --> 09:29.402
-Gosh, so frustrating.
-What do you…

09:29.486 --> 09:30.487
[Mr. Park] Is anyone in?

09:30.570 --> 09:32.238
-[Ms. Hwang] Oh, my!
-[Jucheon] Huh?

09:32.989 --> 09:34.240
[Ms. Hwang] Oh, goodness!

09:35.408 --> 09:36.993
I see you were still eating.

09:37.077 --> 09:38.244
-Hello.
-[Ms. Hwang] Goodness.

09:38.328 --> 09:40.997
You were discharged
from the hospital already?

09:41.081 --> 09:42.165
[chuckling] Yes.

09:42.248 --> 09:45.043
I got treated right away, after all.

09:45.126 --> 09:48.546
-Dr. Do's stubbornness saved my life.
-[Ms. Hwang laughs]

09:48.630 --> 09:53.384
Had it not been for Dr. Do Jiui,
I'd be on my way to Heaven by now.

09:53.468 --> 09:55.178
[Ms. Hwang, Mr. Park chuckling]

09:55.261 --> 09:57.305
[Mr. Park sighs] My, my, my.

09:58.765 --> 10:01.351
[Ms. Hwang exclaims]
Isn't this monkfish liver?

10:01.434 --> 10:02.894
What a precious treat!

10:02.977 --> 10:05.522
Not as precious as my own life.

10:05.605 --> 10:07.440
[Ms. Hwang, Mr. Park chuckling]

10:08.691 --> 10:10.735
Goodness, Dr. Do.

10:11.444 --> 10:13.196
Thank you so much.

10:13.279 --> 10:16.825
Once I make a full recovery,
I'll pay you back for everything.

10:16.908 --> 10:18.368
You can count on it. [laughs]

10:18.451 --> 10:19.494
Okay.

10:20.078 --> 10:22.997
We took too much of your time
when you were eating.

10:23.081 --> 10:25.250
-Let's go now, Chunsik.
-That's right.

10:25.333 --> 10:27.585
You must be tired
since you just got discharged,

10:27.669 --> 10:30.213
-so go home to rest up.
-Okay.

10:30.296 --> 10:32.841
-Thank you, everyone. [chuckles]
-Goodbye.

10:32.924 --> 10:36.594
-Take care.
-[Ms. Hwang] Oh my, thank you.

10:36.678 --> 10:38.930
-Have a safe trip home.
-[Mr. Park] Sure.

10:39.013 --> 10:40.557
I love you, Dr. Do.

10:40.640 --> 10:41.641
What?

10:41.724 --> 10:44.602
You're totally
in the chief's good graces now.

10:45.270 --> 10:47.939
On this island,
once you get on his good side,

10:48.022 --> 10:49.899
your quality of life skyrockets.

10:49.983 --> 10:52.360
Last time, he brought me pizza
from the mainland

10:52.443 --> 10:54.320
because he liked my acupuncture treatment.

10:55.029 --> 10:57.031
[chuckles] I got pizza for acupuncture,

10:57.115 --> 11:00.243
so can you imagine how well
he'd treat you for saving his life?

11:00.326 --> 11:01.411
Pizza?

11:01.494 --> 11:03.788
Just because
he liked your acupuncture treatment?

11:03.872 --> 11:05.415
Yes! Pizza!

11:05.915 --> 11:07.083
[Jiui chuckles]

11:07.167 --> 11:10.128
[♪ playful music plays]

11:11.129 --> 11:12.714
-What the heck?
-[clears throat]
STYLE
::cue()

11:15.175 --> 11:17.927
[sighs] Let's see…

11:24.684 --> 11:25.768
[exclaims]

11:30.648 --> 11:33.067
Ms. Eom. What's going on here?

11:33.151 --> 11:34.277
What now?

11:34.360 --> 11:37.238
I mean your slippers.
They're the same as mine.

11:38.531 --> 11:40.992
Did you pay a premium
for the overseas shipping too?

11:41.075 --> 11:44.078
I heard these were really hard to get.

11:44.954 --> 11:46.748
A premium?

11:48.917 --> 11:49.918
Let me see now.

11:51.044 --> 11:52.045
[exclaims]

11:52.128 --> 11:54.631
Did they always have this color?

11:54.714 --> 11:56.549
I've never seen it before.

11:56.633 --> 11:59.886
What are you, a detective?
What are you looking at my feet for?

12:00.470 --> 12:02.722
I'm just fascinated, that's all.

12:03.389 --> 12:06.017
I think we have pretty similar taste.

12:06.100 --> 12:07.644
Similar, my ass.

12:07.727 --> 12:11.189
How could I possibly have similar taste
to someone who owns a clinic in Seoul?

12:12.357 --> 12:13.650
Just get back to work!

12:14.943 --> 12:16.277
[Ms. Eom huffs]

12:17.528 --> 12:20.782
He's such a weirdo! [sighs]

12:22.116 --> 12:23.409
Damn it!

12:24.953 --> 12:27.997
Who the hell pays a premium
for a flimsy pair of slippers?

12:28.081 --> 12:33.044
I do not like him one bit. [exclaims]

12:40.802 --> 12:42.136
[grunts]

12:43.012 --> 12:44.305
[stomach growling]

12:45.056 --> 12:46.391
[groans]

12:50.353 --> 12:51.646
[groans] I'm so hungry.

12:51.729 --> 12:53.690
[phone chiming]

12:59.362 --> 13:02.824
[doctor 1] It's only 8:00 p.m.,
but none of the stores are open…

13:02.907 --> 13:04.617
[doctor 2] Our island only has
one supermarket.

13:04.701 --> 13:06.369
[doctor 3] Ours doesn't even open
at times.

13:06.452 --> 13:08.913
I realized the value
of convenience stores.

13:08.997 --> 13:11.457
[doctor 4] If you come across these
on your next trip to the market,

13:11.541 --> 13:12.917
you have to stockpile them.

13:13.001 --> 13:17.171
They rarely stock up on beer,
so finders keepers.

13:17.255 --> 13:18.715
[doctor 1] I should rush over there now!

13:18.798 --> 13:20.967
Some beer to keep me company
on these long nights!

13:21.050 --> 13:23.386
Oh, beer…

13:24.929 --> 13:26.639
Beer.

13:28.141 --> 13:29.517
[sighs]

13:31.227 --> 13:34.397
[clicks tongue]
They don't have any ales or IPAs, though.

13:36.816 --> 13:39.277
I wonder if the chief
would get some for me.

13:39.360 --> 13:41.237
[chuckles]

13:41.320 --> 13:44.365
Hey, I got here first.
You can't just take them all like that.

13:44.449 --> 13:46.242
-Hey…
-Granny, put these on my tab!

13:46.325 --> 13:47.368
Okay.

13:47.452 --> 13:48.745
Goodbye!

13:49.454 --> 13:52.206
Excuse me, do you have any more beer?

13:52.290 --> 13:53.458
No, that was it.

13:53.541 --> 13:55.126
Wow, I can't even.

13:56.085 --> 13:57.295
What the hell?

13:57.962 --> 14:00.298
[♪ playful music plays]

14:00.381 --> 14:03.384
LUCKY SUPERMARKET

14:06.763 --> 14:07.930
[Hari] Mmm.

14:09.640 --> 14:11.017
You drink every day?

14:11.684 --> 14:15.021
Man, what's that voice I hear?
It seems to be crossing a line.

14:16.773 --> 14:20.276
You probably shouldn't be drinking.
If you drink like that every day…

14:23.821 --> 14:25.531
It's just bad for you.

14:25.615 --> 14:28.659
I'm guessing that's a roundabout way
of telling me to hand some over.

14:28.743 --> 14:30.453
But stop crossing the line, okay?

14:30.536 --> 14:32.580
-That's not it. I just--
-Hey.

14:35.041 --> 14:36.959
Do you know how suspicious you are?

14:37.960 --> 14:38.961
What do you mean?

14:39.045 --> 14:41.380
I mean, why do we keep
running into each other?

14:42.590 --> 14:43.925
Are you…

14:44.425 --> 14:46.219
a stalker?

14:46.302 --> 14:48.054
[stammers] A stalker?

14:49.514 --> 14:51.974
Listen, you're the one
who's always butting in, okay?

14:52.058 --> 14:54.435
I boarded the ferry first,
and I also came here first.

14:54.519 --> 14:56.145
So if we're talking about stalking,

14:56.229 --> 14:57.980
I'd say you fit the profile more.

14:59.440 --> 15:00.441
If not, never mind.

15:01.901 --> 15:02.902
"If not, never"…

15:05.822 --> 15:06.989
[chuckles, scoffs]

15:10.118 --> 15:13.913
[exclaims, distorted]

15:16.415 --> 15:18.209
[both grunting]

15:25.800 --> 15:27.885
Look at me. I almost crossed the line.

15:29.554 --> 15:30.555
[exclaims]

15:36.394 --> 15:38.771
[groaning]
STYLE
::cue()

15:47.029 --> 15:48.072
[gasps]

15:50.074 --> 15:51.534
What the hell?

15:53.786 --> 15:54.787
Hello.

15:55.371 --> 15:57.957
[Jiui sighs] So she's a nurse.

15:59.000 --> 16:00.793
-[sighs]
-Say hello, everyone.

16:00.877 --> 16:02.545
This is Ms. Yuk Hari.

16:02.628 --> 16:06.549
I'm Eom Jeongseon, a fourth-year nurse.

16:06.632 --> 16:08.718
You're third-year… so, class of '19?

16:08.801 --> 16:10.261
I was in the class of '18.

16:10.344 --> 16:13.681
Yes, class of '19.
I'm sure I have a lot to learn from you.

16:13.764 --> 16:16.142
Right. I look forward to working with you.

16:16.225 --> 16:18.144
[Ms. Hwang]
A lot to learn from her? Please.

16:18.227 --> 16:22.899
Ms. Hari here is an intellectual who used
to work in a university hospital's ER.

16:22.982 --> 16:24.942
Not just any hospital, but Asong Hospital.

16:25.026 --> 16:28.404
I'm sure the operating room
was practically her living room.

16:28.487 --> 16:31.657
But still, isn't this her first time
at a public health center?

16:31.741 --> 16:34.285
Mmm. It may be her first time,

16:34.368 --> 16:37.038
but ever since she was a kid,
she visited the island every holiday,

16:37.121 --> 16:39.457
so she's well-acquainted with Pyeondongdo.

16:39.540 --> 16:43.252
Wow, then you must be
really close to the villagers here.

16:43.336 --> 16:44.670
That's great.

16:44.754 --> 16:47.798
I think it's way harder
to get close to the villagers here

16:47.882 --> 16:49.342
than it is to work here.

16:49.425 --> 16:51.802
That's because you slack off all the time.

16:51.886 --> 16:54.013
I'm Yong Jucheon
of the Korean Medicine Ward.

16:54.096 --> 16:56.682
[Hari chuckles] I look forward
to working with you.

16:56.766 --> 17:00.686
And this here is Dr. Do Jiui, the surgeon.

17:00.770 --> 17:05.358
He's the very man
you busted your ass carrying over here.

17:05.441 --> 17:06.734
[exclaims]

17:07.526 --> 17:09.153
So you're a doctor.

17:09.237 --> 17:10.321
Uh, yes.

17:11.155 --> 17:12.490
[Ms. Hwang] Huh?

17:13.282 --> 17:15.326
Have you already greeted each other?

17:15.409 --> 17:16.702
[chuckles]

17:16.786 --> 17:20.957
Well, I don't know if I can say that.

17:21.040 --> 17:22.625
It might be crossing a line.

17:23.793 --> 17:25.503
[Ms. Hwang] What are you talking about?

17:29.131 --> 17:30.258
I'm Hyeon Chiyeon.

17:31.050 --> 17:32.843
I look forward to working with you.

17:33.511 --> 17:35.888
Now then, doctors,
please get ready to see patients.

17:35.972 --> 17:37.598
-Okay.
-As for us,

17:37.682 --> 17:40.351
let me just pull you aside
for a quick chat. This way.

17:41.143 --> 17:42.770
[Hyeon] Never expected to see her here.

17:43.271 --> 17:45.606
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

17:45.690 --> 17:47.775
[Ms. Hwang, Hari chuckling]

17:47.858 --> 17:53.155
My, you used to be so tiny,
but you've grown so much.

17:53.239 --> 17:56.576
But why did you come here
from such a good university hospital?

17:57.201 --> 17:58.202
Ah…

17:58.953 --> 18:00.454
Well…

18:00.538 --> 18:04.417
I was just wondering why you came
all the way to this island from the city.

18:04.500 --> 18:05.960
If there was a story behind it.

18:07.253 --> 18:10.131
-I just wanted to take a break.
-Mmm.

18:10.840 --> 18:12.216
Take a break?

18:12.300 --> 18:13.384
Right.

18:13.467 --> 18:14.927
Let's do that.

18:15.011 --> 18:17.597
-Take it slow and easy.
-[Hari] Mmm.

18:17.680 --> 18:19.098
-[chuckles]
-[phone ringing]

18:19.181 --> 18:22.518
-Let's catch up again later.
-Uh-huh.

18:22.602 --> 18:23.728
[ringing stops]

18:23.811 --> 18:27.148
This is Hwang Sinhye from
the Public Health Center speaking.

18:27.231 --> 18:33.279
Though working here may look peaceful,
it's actually a war zone,

18:33.362 --> 18:37.491
and the work we do is just as complicated
as working in an operating room.

18:37.575 --> 18:40.161
It's not the kind of place
where you can just take a break,

18:40.244 --> 18:41.912
is all I'm saying.

18:41.996 --> 18:44.874
I see. [chuckles]
I look forward to your guidance.

18:44.957 --> 18:46.208
-Mm-hmm.
-Ah!

18:46.292 --> 18:47.668
What should I do first?

18:48.919 --> 18:49.920
Ooh…

18:51.213 --> 18:52.214
[stammers]

18:52.298 --> 18:55.551
Why don't you start by switching out
the toilet paper rolls in the bathroom?

18:56.135 --> 18:57.136
Ah…

18:58.012 --> 18:59.013
Toilet paper?

19:01.432 --> 19:03.267
Okay. [chuckles]

19:04.226 --> 19:05.728
-This way?
-Mm-hmm.

19:05.811 --> 19:07.396
[Ms. Hwang chattering]

19:10.900 --> 19:14.403
Why on earth did I mention toilet paper,
after putting on such a front?

19:15.112 --> 19:16.113
[gasps]

19:20.785 --> 19:22.578
[sighs]

19:22.662 --> 19:23.829
[mouse clicking]

19:24.914 --> 19:26.082
[no audible dialogue]

19:34.048 --> 19:35.299
[sighs]

19:35.383 --> 19:37.051
Of all people, why…

19:38.219 --> 19:40.971
Dr. Jiui, you're going to
have to go somewhere.

19:41.055 --> 19:43.557
It's a patient who just had
a cancer operation,

19:43.641 --> 19:45.643
but his daughter's
having trouble reaching him.

19:45.726 --> 19:47.561
She's asking if we can check in on him.

19:48.729 --> 19:51.440
-Me?
-Who else? Should I go?

19:51.524 --> 19:53.192
I don't know my way around yet.

19:53.275 --> 19:56.195
Don't worry about that.
We'll send another person with you.

19:56.779 --> 19:58.447
All settled, right? Mm-mmm.

19:58.531 --> 19:59.699
[♪ playful music plays]

20:00.950 --> 20:01.992
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

20:11.627 --> 20:13.587
[metal creaking]

20:15.423 --> 20:16.841
Oh, gosh.

20:20.428 --> 20:22.596
[boat approaching]

20:34.150 --> 20:35.317
Easy, easy!

20:37.403 --> 20:38.446
Seriously…

20:39.155 --> 20:40.156
Hello!

20:40.239 --> 20:42.450
[captain] Hey!
Looks like it's starting to drizzle.

20:42.533 --> 20:43.617
[Hari] I know, right?

20:43.701 --> 20:46.495
Sir, you said it was nearby.
Why do we need a boat?

20:46.579 --> 20:48.831
It's only five minutes away by boat.

20:49.498 --> 20:50.541
Oh, come on…

20:50.624 --> 20:52.168
[captain] What business do you have there?

20:52.251 --> 20:54.754
A patient's guardian
requested a home visit.

20:54.837 --> 20:56.839
A patient on that side? Who's sick?

20:56.922 --> 20:58.424
Do you know Mr. Kim Jeongbae?

20:58.507 --> 21:00.217
Kim Jeongbae? Who could that be?

21:01.051 --> 21:03.053
Oh, that guy?

21:03.137 --> 21:05.681
I guess it's the guy who keeps to himself.

21:05.765 --> 21:08.642
But I don't think it'll be easy
getting in that house.

21:09.226 --> 21:12.688
The guy seemed to really hate
people entering his house.

21:13.272 --> 21:14.356
Oh…

21:14.440 --> 21:16.567
So he hates it when people cross the line,

21:17.401 --> 21:18.652
like someone I know.

21:19.153 --> 21:20.154
[captain] What?

21:20.237 --> 21:22.865
Ah, it's nothing.
We can go there now, right?

21:22.948 --> 21:24.992
-Of course. Get in.
-[stammers] Wait.

21:26.202 --> 21:28.996
[stammers] Isn't there
some other way there?

21:29.079 --> 21:30.539
Some other way?

21:31.874 --> 21:34.126
Well, they are connected.

21:34.210 --> 21:37.505
But if you were to walk,
it would take at least 40 minutes.

21:37.588 --> 21:39.924
With the mountain path
being really hilly and all. [laughs]

21:40.007 --> 21:42.802
Who would be dumb enough to do that?

21:42.885 --> 21:44.470
[captain, Hari laugh]

21:44.553 --> 21:47.097
Forty minutes? Okay.

21:47.765 --> 21:50.559
Wait, Dr. Do. You're going to walk there?

21:50.643 --> 21:53.562
You take the boat.
I'll walk. See you there.

21:53.646 --> 21:55.648
Wait… [stammering]

21:55.731 --> 21:57.274
Doctor!

21:57.858 --> 22:00.236
[♪ playful music plays]

22:00.319 --> 22:02.738
Where the heck am I? Damn it.

22:04.990 --> 22:06.700
[panting]

22:08.327 --> 22:09.787
[Hari] Hey, wait up.

22:14.834 --> 22:17.044
[panting] We could have been there
in five minutes.

22:17.127 --> 22:18.963
Why punish ourselves by walking there?

22:19.046 --> 22:21.674
I never asked you to come with me, okay?

22:21.757 --> 22:23.884
You could have just taken the boat.

22:23.968 --> 22:26.637
It's not like there's anything I can do
without a doctor.

22:26.720 --> 22:28.681
Why should I go there by myself?

22:31.308 --> 22:32.309
I was talking to myself.

22:35.104 --> 22:38.023
Tells me not to cross the line
but gives me so many causes for concern.

22:38.107 --> 22:39.733
-Ms. Yuk.
-Okay, okay.

22:39.817 --> 22:41.485
I'll stop talking to myself.

22:41.569 --> 22:44.154
Hurry up. [groans]

22:53.956 --> 22:56.959
Haven't you been here before, Ms. Hari?

22:57.042 --> 22:59.295
Who would walk here?
Everyone takes a boat.

23:00.754 --> 23:01.755
Let me see.

23:05.634 --> 23:07.261
[insect chittering]

23:07.344 --> 23:08.596
[screams]

23:09.847 --> 23:11.140
Hey, will you please…

23:11.724 --> 23:14.184
That's not it. Your shoulder, Dr. Do…

23:15.144 --> 23:16.186
What about my shoulder?

23:16.270 --> 23:17.271
The other side…

23:18.647 --> 23:19.690
What is it?

23:20.274 --> 23:22.818
Uh… You know what? Never mind.

23:22.902 --> 23:26.196
You think helping is crossing a line,
so I'm not going to say anything.

23:27.573 --> 23:30.034
-But that's going to bite, though.
-What?

23:31.994 --> 23:34.288
[exclaiming]

23:34.872 --> 23:37.750
Don't move. It's venomous.

23:37.833 --> 23:41.253
Help me with this. Now!

23:41.337 --> 23:45.507
I want to help, but I have to be careful.

23:45.591 --> 23:46.759
What?

23:47.343 --> 23:49.553
You see,
I learned something thanks to you.

23:49.637 --> 23:51.931
No matter how much someone's struggling,

23:52.014 --> 23:55.184
helping when they don't ask for it
is crossing a line.

23:55.267 --> 23:57.853
It's trying to get in!

23:57.937 --> 23:59.104
Hurry and do something!

23:59.188 --> 24:00.898
What can I do? I can't cross the line.

24:01.982 --> 24:04.026
-[stammers] Cross it.
-What?

24:04.109 --> 24:06.445
Please cross the line!

24:07.029 --> 24:08.614
-Damn it…
-Cross it?

24:08.697 --> 24:11.241
-Cross it. It just crawled inside!
-[exclaims]

24:11.325 --> 24:12.868
-Get it out.
-Just so we're clear,

24:12.952 --> 24:14.244
you said to cross it.

24:14.328 --> 24:16.997
Put your hands inside and take it out.

24:17.081 --> 24:19.041
It's way inside!

24:19.124 --> 24:20.709
-Lower!
-Where? Okay.

24:20.793 --> 24:22.753
-Oh, come on!
-Okay.

24:22.836 --> 24:25.172
-[Jiui exclaims]
-[Hari grunting]

24:25.255 --> 24:27.758
-It's not there. What?
-Uh, Ms. Hari, it went down.

24:27.841 --> 24:28.842
Right now…

24:28.926 --> 24:31.595
-Left waist!
-Darn it!
STYLE
::cue()

24:31.679 --> 24:32.888
-[gasps]
-[Hari] Stand still!

24:32.972 --> 24:34.431
[Jiui] Oh, come on!

24:34.515 --> 24:36.558
[exclaims] I think it bit me.

24:36.642 --> 24:37.643
That was my nail.

24:38.978 --> 24:40.771
Stop playing around, seriously!

24:40.854 --> 24:42.022
I'm not.

24:42.106 --> 24:45.109
-[breathing heavily]
-Oh, oh! Here it is. Hold still.

24:46.151 --> 24:47.987
-I caught it.
-You caught it?

24:49.738 --> 24:51.156
[exclaims]

24:51.240 --> 24:52.950
Shouldn't we trap that guy somewhere?

24:53.033 --> 24:55.244
You said it's venomous.
What if it bites someone?

24:55.327 --> 24:56.829
-Why would we do that?
-Damn it.

24:56.912 --> 24:59.331
-They don't bite if you leave them alone.
-[sighs]

25:01.709 --> 25:04.628
Dr. Do, you owe me one now.
Pay me back later.

25:07.297 --> 25:08.590
But…

25:08.674 --> 25:10.259
But that guy's venomous.

25:12.886 --> 25:15.431
Its fangs were terrifying. Did you see?

25:15.514 --> 25:17.599
[thunder rumbling]

25:20.185 --> 25:23.105
[Jiui panting]

25:23.188 --> 25:24.982
This place…

25:27.735 --> 25:29.111
[both groan]

25:29.194 --> 25:30.529
[Jiui] This is…

25:36.368 --> 25:38.996
Uh, are you sure this is the place?

25:39.079 --> 25:40.831
It doesn't look like anyone lives here.

25:40.914 --> 25:43.042
This has to be the place.

25:44.793 --> 25:46.503
Just a second.

25:46.587 --> 25:47.671
[Hari grunts]

25:47.755 --> 25:49.882
DO NOT ENTER

25:49.965 --> 25:51.633
[door creaks]

25:51.717 --> 25:55.929
Mr. Kim Jeongbae,
we're here from the public health center.

25:57.264 --> 25:59.099
Mr. Kim Jeongbae, are you home?

26:02.478 --> 26:04.563
I'm pretty sure this is the place.

26:05.814 --> 26:07.691
Hold on.

26:07.775 --> 26:10.736
[stammers] Are you going in?
That would be a bad idea.

26:11.320 --> 26:14.031
She said it's a patient
who was treated for cancer recently.

26:15.074 --> 26:18.494
If you're going to cross any lines,
you have to make it count.

26:18.577 --> 26:20.162
Especially when saving someone.

26:22.372 --> 26:23.707
[stammers, grunts]

26:29.463 --> 26:31.548
-[thunder rumbling]
-Oh, man…

26:32.299 --> 26:34.176
Hey, Ms. Yuk?

26:34.259 --> 26:36.345
It doesn't look like anyone's here,

26:36.428 --> 26:38.138
so let's come back for them next time.

26:38.222 --> 26:40.182
-Mr. Kim Jeongbae!
-Come on.

26:40.724 --> 26:42.267
Mr. Kim Jeongbae?

26:45.270 --> 26:46.271
Let's go inside.

26:46.355 --> 26:48.190
Wait, Ms. Yuk. Why would you go in there?

26:48.273 --> 26:50.526
How dare you enter my home
without permission?

26:52.653 --> 26:53.821
Who the hell are you?

26:54.655 --> 26:56.573
We're from the Public Health Center.

26:56.657 --> 26:59.493
Your daughter said
she couldn't get in touch with you--

26:59.576 --> 27:00.994
Get lost!

27:01.745 --> 27:02.830
Yes, sir.

27:04.665 --> 27:08.168
Now that we know he's fine, let's go.
Hurry up.

27:08.252 --> 27:11.213
Since we're here,
how about a simple checkup? I think that…

27:11.296 --> 27:13.090
What else do we need to check?

27:13.173 --> 27:14.591
…would be a good idea.

27:17.261 --> 27:18.262
But…

27:18.887 --> 27:20.389
he's smoking.

27:23.392 --> 27:25.018
[♪ somber music plays]

27:25.102 --> 27:26.103
Sir.

27:26.770 --> 27:31.358
I heard you recently had surgery,
but you're smoking right now.

27:31.441 --> 27:35.404
That's why your daughter was so worried
and called us.

27:37.531 --> 27:38.532
So what?

27:39.157 --> 27:41.076
Get the hell out before you regret it.

27:43.245 --> 27:45.622
-[lighter clicks]
-We have to go, Ms. Yuk.

27:45.706 --> 27:48.000
-I feel sorry for your daughter.
-Ms. Yuk?

27:49.042 --> 27:52.546
She's been losing sleep over her dad,
who doesn't even care about his own life.

27:52.629 --> 27:54.882
Why get the surgery
if you're going to act like this?

27:59.344 --> 28:01.930
I'm going to contact your daughter.

28:02.014 --> 28:04.266
She needs to know
what kind of state her dad's in.

28:04.349 --> 28:07.728
That way, she'll get to decide
whether to give up on her dad or not.

28:14.860 --> 28:18.030
[♪ tense music plays]

28:18.113 --> 28:20.449
Say one word to my daughter,

28:20.532 --> 28:22.242
-and I'll really kill you.
-Whoa! Sir!

28:22.326 --> 28:24.828
I guess you are ashamed,
seeing as you're angry.

28:24.912 --> 28:26.997
[Jiui] We're sorry. Come with me, Ms. Yuk.

28:27.080 --> 28:28.790
-Sorry, sir.
-I'm not done talking!

28:28.874 --> 28:30.709
-[Jiui] Hurry up!
-[Hari] What are you doing?

28:30.792 --> 28:32.711
What's wrong with you?

28:33.378 --> 28:34.963
-What?
-Come with me.

28:35.047 --> 28:36.840
What on earth are you doing right now?

28:36.924 --> 28:37.925
What?

28:38.008 --> 28:42.137
Don't you know that bringing up smoking
with a cancer patient only riles them up?

28:42.220 --> 28:43.889
I'm just frustrated!

28:46.224 --> 28:47.392
Why would it make you…

28:48.852 --> 28:50.062
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

28:50.145 --> 28:53.315
[owl hooting]

28:53.398 --> 28:55.233
[insects chittering]

28:59.571 --> 29:02.741
Hey, what was that about earlier?

29:06.078 --> 29:08.288
That man still has a chance.

29:10.332 --> 29:15.212
How could someone try so hard
to ruin a second chance at life like that?

29:16.046 --> 29:19.049
Not everyone can get a second chance.

29:19.841 --> 29:23.387
Some people try their hardest to live,
but end up dying anyway.

29:24.554 --> 29:26.431
If I were that man…

29:27.933 --> 29:30.143
I'd try to live seeing only good things,

29:30.227 --> 29:32.437
doing good deeds,
and thinking good thoughts.

29:34.064 --> 29:35.607
So I can live for a long time.

29:36.817 --> 29:39.695
[♪ mournful music plays]

29:46.618 --> 29:48.704
CHAVOXIFEN
CHAVOXIFEN CITRATE

29:55.127 --> 29:57.254
[Jiui stammers] There must be a way.

29:57.337 --> 29:58.922
There's no such thing.

29:59.756 --> 30:01.508
That's not true. It's too soon to--

30:01.591 --> 30:03.677
What can we do now? The sun's gone down.

30:03.760 --> 30:05.887
-[animal howls in distance]
-What?

30:05.971 --> 30:08.473
I think we're lost.

30:09.516 --> 30:11.268
-What?
-[bird squawks]

30:11.351 --> 30:13.103
-Oh, crap! [sighs]
-Right?

30:15.397 --> 30:17.399
[animal howls in distance]

30:17.482 --> 30:18.692
[Jiui] Huh?

30:18.775 --> 30:20.193
What do we do?

30:20.277 --> 30:22.529
Why are you asking me that?

30:22.612 --> 30:25.115
-[♪ mysterious music plays]
-Oh, man…

30:25.198 --> 30:26.700
-[rustling]
-[bird squawks]

30:26.783 --> 30:28.452
[both gasp]

30:29.911 --> 30:30.912
Oh…

30:33.874 --> 30:35.000
-[exclaims]
-[rattling]

30:35.083 --> 30:36.501
-What is that?
-What is it?

30:36.585 --> 30:38.462
Never mind.
I thought it was something else.

30:38.545 --> 30:39.546
Come on!

30:43.008 --> 30:45.927
Aim the flashlight properly!

30:46.011 --> 30:47.971
You should be aiming it properly, okay?

30:48.055 --> 30:51.767
Didn't you learn in science class
that you're supposed to raise it high

30:51.850 --> 30:53.810
so that the light spreads more?

30:53.894 --> 30:54.895
Darn it…

30:54.978 --> 30:59.024
How can you talk science when you
can't even see what's under your feet?

31:00.484 --> 31:02.235
Are you sure we're going the right way?

31:02.903 --> 31:03.904
Oh…

31:04.488 --> 31:07.407
I think I saw this tree earlier.

31:08.825 --> 31:10.952
Is this place haunted by ghosts?

31:11.495 --> 31:14.331
That's strange.
I thought we were going the right way.

31:14.414 --> 31:16.249
[stammers] Ghosts?

31:17.417 --> 31:18.627
Yes, ghosts.

31:18.710 --> 31:20.504
Oh, come on! You scared me!

31:21.171 --> 31:23.590
Is my face really that scary?

31:23.673 --> 31:25.550
I've seen worse, but I'm bearing with it.

31:27.761 --> 31:31.264
[breathing heavily] I don't think
we'll find our way out at this rate.

31:31.348 --> 31:32.891
Let's split up and look around.

31:34.184 --> 31:35.185
Hey.

31:35.268 --> 31:36.728
[wind howling]

31:36.812 --> 31:38.105
Ms. Yuk!

31:38.188 --> 31:41.441
Uh, split up? I don't want to! [groans]

31:42.275 --> 31:44.945
[stammers] I don't want that.
Let's stay together.

31:45.028 --> 31:47.614
We won't find the way like this, so--

31:47.697 --> 31:49.116
Let's just stay together.

31:52.035 --> 31:53.453
Is it because you're scared?

31:56.832 --> 31:57.833
[sighs]

31:57.916 --> 32:01.711
Wow, it's one thing
after another with you.

32:01.795 --> 32:03.922
-[stammers, grunts]
-[vehicle approaches]

32:04.965 --> 32:06.550
-Oh…
-Huh?

32:18.145 --> 32:21.231
-[Hari gasps] Dr. Chiyeon!
-What are you doing here?

32:22.107 --> 32:23.567
You didn't return, so here I am.

32:24.276 --> 32:26.945
With the sun setting
and the boats no longer running.

32:27.028 --> 32:30.240
-[gasps, chuckles]
-[sighs] Man, I'm so relieved.

32:31.658 --> 32:32.868
[Hari chuckles]

32:39.374 --> 32:40.584
-Hop on.
-Okay.

32:44.212 --> 32:47.340
Oh… How should I get on?

32:49.342 --> 32:50.719
Should I get on down there?

32:51.344 --> 32:52.804
Okay. Sure.

32:52.888 --> 32:54.222
Keep backing up.

32:54.306 --> 32:56.433
Good, just like that.

32:56.516 --> 32:58.476
Yes, just keep backing up.

33:00.437 --> 33:01.980
But are you sure I can get on?
STYLE
::cue()

33:02.063 --> 33:03.732
I don't think I'd fit.

33:03.815 --> 33:05.901
Another ride will come.
This is a two-seater.

33:06.610 --> 33:09.279
-Wait a second!
-I'll see you later.

33:09.905 --> 33:11.489
[Jiui] I said wait a second!

33:11.573 --> 33:12.824
Take me with you!

33:14.075 --> 33:15.076
Hey!

33:16.244 --> 33:17.370
I'm scared!

33:17.454 --> 33:18.538
Come on.

33:25.337 --> 33:27.088
Are you sure he'll be okay?

33:27.172 --> 33:28.840
He seems to be a scaredy-cat.

33:28.924 --> 33:30.217
He's a big boy.

33:31.468 --> 33:33.261
-Hold on tight.
-What?

33:34.262 --> 33:35.347
Oh, okay.

33:39.309 --> 33:41.937
-Not there. I meant the handles.
-What?

33:43.980 --> 33:46.358
Oh. Um, uh, right.

33:48.443 --> 33:50.862
You still have a habit
of jumping to conclusions.

33:51.905 --> 33:53.323
Excuse me?

33:53.406 --> 33:55.158
Do you really not remember me?

33:57.827 --> 33:58.912
Wait.

34:08.213 --> 34:09.506
Oh… [chuckles]

34:10.340 --> 34:11.341
I'm sorry.

34:12.092 --> 34:13.510
What?

34:13.593 --> 34:14.970
I have a boyfriend.

34:16.304 --> 34:18.890
-Hey, wait--
-I told you I have a boyfriend.

34:19.391 --> 34:22.727
[♪ comedic music plays]

34:29.025 --> 34:30.360
CLIFFSIDE RAW FISH RESTAURANT

34:33.154 --> 34:34.155
[Hyeon sighs]

34:35.657 --> 34:37.909
Just tell me, okay?

34:40.370 --> 34:41.579
If you buy me a meal.

34:42.205 --> 34:43.206
What?

34:44.457 --> 34:47.919
[exclaims] Come on. We've met before?

34:56.928 --> 34:58.346
-Hello.
-[owner] You're here?

34:58.430 --> 34:59.514
-Hey.
-Auntie!

35:00.974 --> 35:02.183
[gasps]

35:02.267 --> 35:03.351
Dr. Do.

35:06.021 --> 35:07.731
How did you get here so fast?

35:09.065 --> 35:10.066
Thanks to you…

35:10.859 --> 35:12.527
I almost ended up dying, okay?

35:13.361 --> 35:14.362
[retches]

35:16.072 --> 35:18.366
[yelps] Ma'am, go slower!

35:18.450 --> 35:20.035
Go slower! [yells]

35:22.954 --> 35:24.122
[screams]

35:24.205 --> 35:26.207
Slower!

35:27.000 --> 35:29.419
[screams]

35:29.502 --> 35:32.839
It was seriously a white-knuckle ride.

35:32.922 --> 35:34.966
Cheer… [grunts] …up!

35:35.050 --> 35:36.134
Here.

35:37.427 --> 35:38.428
You're drinking?

35:39.137 --> 35:41.222
You're meant to drink on days like this.

35:42.098 --> 35:43.475
[owner] You're here?

35:43.558 --> 35:44.976
-[Jangsu] Yes.
-Hey, welcome.

35:45.644 --> 35:46.645
What's this?

35:47.812 --> 35:49.189
Oh, my.

35:49.272 --> 35:52.525
I see Dr. Stickler was here.

35:52.609 --> 35:55.445
The great doctor who won't give
proper prescriptions

35:55.528 --> 35:57.864
because he suspects
his patients of foul play.

35:57.947 --> 35:59.324
That's right.

36:00.283 --> 36:05.455
You see, just like you have your rules,

36:05.538 --> 36:08.124
we have our own rules here in Pyeondongdo.

36:08.750 --> 36:10.377
For every new arrival,

36:10.460 --> 36:14.130
our youth association determines
who's the senior and the junior

36:14.214 --> 36:16.716
by having a drink-off.

36:17.342 --> 36:19.844
Whoever gets wasted first
becomes the junior,

36:19.928 --> 36:22.681
and must obey the senior's every word.

36:23.264 --> 36:24.474
See where this is going?

36:25.266 --> 36:27.811
That's why the owner here
is my big sister now.

36:27.894 --> 36:30.230
-Right.
-Geumja, my sis!

36:30.313 --> 36:31.314
Gosh, that's so gross.

36:31.398 --> 36:33.983
[Jangsu, captain chuckling]

36:35.068 --> 36:38.613
What do you say?
Would you, Dr. Stickler-for-the-Rules,

36:38.697 --> 36:42.492
like to partake in our ritual
so we can establish a proper hierarchy?

36:45.120 --> 36:46.121
Well…

36:46.204 --> 36:49.082
I guess he doesn't have
what it takes. [chuckles]

36:49.165 --> 36:50.959
Is it because all he's done is study?

36:51.042 --> 36:53.503
He's a total nerd. [laughs]

36:56.047 --> 36:57.966
-Let's just go.
-Yeah, let's go.

36:58.550 --> 37:01.094
We have to get back quickly--

37:01.177 --> 37:03.221
If those are the rules here,
I'll give it a go.

37:04.222 --> 37:05.807
Dr. Do, no…

37:06.474 --> 37:07.809
You mean it?

37:08.309 --> 37:09.602
Yes.

37:11.020 --> 37:12.021
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

37:15.275 --> 37:18.611
Those guys, they're not human
when it comes to booze, okay?

37:19.154 --> 37:21.364
They're hounds. Boozehounds.

37:22.490 --> 37:24.367
Gosh, I'm so worried.

37:26.202 --> 37:29.497
A man should be able to drink this much.
Don't you think so?

37:40.633 --> 37:41.801
[sighs]

37:44.512 --> 37:45.972
[Jangsu scoffs, pants]

37:46.639 --> 37:48.475
This here's a creamy soju.

37:59.736 --> 38:00.737
[Jiui sighs]

38:13.333 --> 38:14.626
[gags]

38:14.709 --> 38:15.794
[retches]

38:19.380 --> 38:21.216
-[Jiui sighs]
-[grunts]

38:21.966 --> 38:23.092
-[Jiui sighs]
-[grunts]

38:23.176 --> 38:26.763
I'm not like him.

38:26.846 --> 38:27.847
Not bad.

38:28.348 --> 38:29.933
You can actually hold your liquor.

38:35.855 --> 38:38.441
-[sighs, grunts]
-[sighs, grunts]

38:40.109 --> 38:41.861
You haven't forgotten, have you?

38:41.945 --> 38:43.321
The rules in Pyeondongdo.

38:43.404 --> 38:46.115
Whoever loses this
has to become an obedient little bro.

38:46.199 --> 38:49.035
I'm very curious

38:49.118 --> 38:53.581
how much of an obedient little bro
Dr. Stickler over here will be

38:53.665 --> 38:55.291
once I beat him.

38:55.375 --> 38:57.502
[chortles]

39:06.970 --> 39:07.971
[gags]

39:09.430 --> 39:10.431
[glass thuds]

39:11.224 --> 39:15.520
[Jangsu groans, retches]

39:15.603 --> 39:17.021
[Jiui] I'm also curious…

39:17.647 --> 39:19.440
[clamoring]

39:19.524 --> 39:21.192
[spectator] Wow, look at him go!

39:21.276 --> 39:22.819
…what I'm like when I'm drunk.

39:22.902 --> 39:29.200
2013 HANGUK UNIVERSITY
PRE-MED SEMESTER KICK-OFF PARTY

39:30.034 --> 39:33.037
[♪ triumphant music plays]

39:38.710 --> 39:39.794
[Geumja] He won.

39:40.336 --> 39:41.671
He actually won.

39:43.131 --> 39:44.841
-[gasps]
-[Hari] Mm-hmm.

39:47.468 --> 39:48.469
Another?

39:49.262 --> 39:51.264
[panting]

39:53.600 --> 39:56.352
[exclaims, slurring] What the…

39:57.061 --> 39:58.521
Do you know who I am?

39:59.522 --> 40:02.108
I'm the Bloodstained Fist
of Pyeondongdo, you prick!

40:06.487 --> 40:07.697
Huh?

40:07.780 --> 40:09.657
[whimpers] Blood…

40:13.786 --> 40:14.871
[whimpers]

40:16.122 --> 40:17.165
[groans]

40:28.801 --> 40:31.763
[groans, slurring] What's this?

40:31.846 --> 40:34.057
What happened to my hand?

40:41.022 --> 40:42.482
Forceps, please. [sighs]

40:46.444 --> 40:47.445
[Jangsu groans]

40:49.238 --> 40:51.574
[groaning]

40:51.658 --> 40:53.618
Looks like you can feel your hand.

40:53.701 --> 40:54.953
[Hari] What should we do?

40:55.620 --> 40:59.040
I think we can stitch him up.
There doesn't seem to be any nerve damage.

40:59.707 --> 41:01.292
You're going to stitch him up?

41:02.085 --> 41:05.213
Out of the question. We had alcohol.

41:05.296 --> 41:07.590
This could cause huge problems
down the line,
STYLE
::cue()

41:07.674 --> 41:09.509
and it has happened before.

41:12.929 --> 41:16.474
Article 7 of the code of medical ethics.
A physician shall not practice medicine

41:16.557 --> 41:19.560
while under the influence
of alcohol, narcotics, or drugs,

41:19.644 --> 41:23.022
or in a physical or mental state
that may cause harm to the patient's life

41:23.815 --> 41:24.941
or physical well-being.

41:25.024 --> 41:27.527
If they complain later
that a drunk doctor operated on him,

41:27.610 --> 41:29.278
you'll both be in big trouble.

41:30.989 --> 41:33.199
Let's have him go
to the hospital early tomorrow.

41:33.282 --> 41:35.410
[snoring]

41:36.411 --> 41:38.287
He definitely won't go.

41:39.163 --> 41:40.915
The boats head out tomorrow,

41:41.541 --> 41:44.711
and missing just a single day
is a huge loss in anchovy fishing.

41:45.837 --> 41:47.088
But he still needs… [sighs]

41:47.171 --> 41:50.591
[snoring continues]

41:51.384 --> 41:53.511
[inhales sharply]
Let's do it tomorrow morning.

41:53.594 --> 41:55.471
It just needs to be done within 24 hours.

41:55.555 --> 41:58.891
For the record, I clearly warned you
that this may cause problems later.

41:58.975 --> 42:01.561
Don't worry. I'll take responsibility.

42:06.441 --> 42:07.567
You should go home too.

42:11.779 --> 42:14.782
[♪ contemplative music plays]

42:46.314 --> 42:47.315
[Hari] Dr. Do.

42:50.985 --> 42:51.986
Dr. Do.

42:52.987 --> 42:53.988
Yes…

42:54.697 --> 42:55.698
Yes?

42:55.782 --> 42:58.367
Um, it's been eight hours.

42:58.451 --> 43:00.828
Don't you think we're good to start now?

43:00.912 --> 43:03.247
Let's treat him quickly
so you can get some rest too.

43:04.707 --> 43:07.293
You're still here? Why?

43:08.336 --> 43:10.171
Because we still have a patient.

44:04.100 --> 44:05.977
Doesn't he get on your nerves?

44:08.187 --> 44:09.522
He filed a complaint,

44:09.605 --> 44:12.900
forced you to drink alcohol,
and picked on you.

44:12.984 --> 44:15.444
Um… [sighs]

44:15.528 --> 44:16.946
You're right. I don't like him.

44:17.029 --> 44:18.948
[inhales sharply] But…

44:20.366 --> 44:21.868
like him or not,

44:22.994 --> 44:24.662
lacerations are lacerations.

44:26.497 --> 44:27.707
Oh…

44:33.296 --> 44:34.922
[exclaims]

44:35.006 --> 44:36.424
What now?

44:37.300 --> 44:38.301
[Hari chuckles]

44:40.011 --> 44:42.180
-[exclaims]
-[chuckles]

44:42.263 --> 44:44.849
[both laugh]

44:46.058 --> 44:47.059
[sniffles]
STYLE
::cue()

45:03.242 --> 45:05.328
[Jangsu] What the heck is this?

45:05.411 --> 45:08.539
What on earth happened to my hand?

45:10.208 --> 45:12.501
You were drunk yesterday
and broke a mirror,

45:12.585 --> 45:14.212
so I stitched up the wounds.

45:14.295 --> 45:17.006
Me? Drunk?

45:18.466 --> 45:21.552
Get a load of this hotshot from Seoul,

45:21.636 --> 45:23.429
blaming me for something I didn't do!

45:23.512 --> 45:25.723
My boat's heading out today!

45:25.806 --> 45:28.684
How am I supposed to
pull the nets with my hand like this?

45:29.560 --> 45:31.854
I won't let this slide, okay?

45:31.938 --> 45:36.067
I'm going to sue you
for also causing me emotional--

45:36.150 --> 45:38.527
What are you going to do
if you don't let it slide?

45:38.611 --> 45:39.612
[Ms. Hwang] Mr. Park!

45:40.780 --> 45:43.157
Everyone knows
you become an animal when you drink.

45:43.241 --> 45:44.700
I'm so sick of this.

45:44.784 --> 45:46.911
Why come all this way
to bitch at the doctors

45:46.994 --> 45:48.955
who are performing their sacred duties?

45:49.038 --> 45:51.457
-No, that's not--
-Don't talk back to your chief.

45:53.000 --> 45:55.461
Pulling the chief card on me.

45:55.544 --> 45:56.712
Like you always do.

45:56.796 --> 45:58.130
[Mr. Park sighs]

45:58.714 --> 46:00.716
-Dr. Do Jiui, come over here.
-Oh.

46:01.342 --> 46:02.343
What's this?

46:02.426 --> 46:05.263
[Mr. Park] This right here is maeuntang.

46:05.346 --> 46:07.181
-[Ms. Hwang] Oh, goodness.
-[Mr. Park chuckles]

46:07.265 --> 46:09.892
It's made with all-natural ingredients,
so it'll be delicious.

46:09.976 --> 46:11.310
You should have it for lunch.

46:11.394 --> 46:12.603
Thank you, sir.

46:12.687 --> 46:13.688
[Mr. Park] All right, then.

46:13.771 --> 46:15.523
-Good luck today.
-Thank you.

46:16.524 --> 46:18.025
Stop interfering and come with me.

46:18.651 --> 46:20.820
Chop-chop! Leave.

46:20.903 --> 46:21.904
Come on.

46:23.322 --> 46:24.448
[chuckles]

46:24.532 --> 46:25.533
-Let's go.
-Hey!

46:25.616 --> 46:27.493
-[Ms. Hwang chuckles]
-Thank you, sir!

46:27.576 --> 46:29.620
-[Mr. Park] Bye!
-[Ms. Hwang] Take care!

46:30.997 --> 46:31.998
[Mr. Park] Okay!

46:32.915 --> 46:36.752
[Hari] I think Mr. Lee Jangsu acted out
like that because he was embarrassed.

46:41.632 --> 46:42.800
[Jiui sighs]

46:44.260 --> 46:48.431
He was defeated
in the chief elections for years,

46:48.514 --> 46:52.310
and now he's even lost his title
as the heaviest drinker to you.

46:53.686 --> 46:55.521
But still, taking it out on me…

46:56.814 --> 46:58.357
It's not like it'll solve anything.

47:00.484 --> 47:04.322
It may not solve anything,
but it can mask your embarrassment.

47:05.781 --> 47:08.951
Isn't that the easiest way out
when you want to hide something?

47:09.035 --> 47:10.453
Getting angry.

47:10.536 --> 47:12.538
[♪ contemplative music plays]

47:13.873 --> 47:15.166
[inhales sharply]

47:15.249 --> 47:16.250
In that case…

47:32.016 --> 47:33.768
What do you think Mr. Kim Jeongbae…

47:35.936 --> 47:37.480
wanted to hide?

47:38.689 --> 47:39.690
What?

47:44.445 --> 47:47.073
-I'm going to go see Mr. Kim Jeongbae.
-Me too!

47:47.156 --> 47:48.532
Dr. Do!

47:48.616 --> 47:50.659
What the heck? Are they BFFs already?

47:52.953 --> 47:55.039
[panting]

47:55.122 --> 47:57.166
[thunderclap]

47:59.960 --> 48:01.545
Mr. Kim Jeongbae!

48:02.880 --> 48:04.090
Mr. Kim Jeongbae!

48:05.716 --> 48:06.759
Damn it.

48:07.760 --> 48:10.596
[thunder rumbling]

48:10.679 --> 48:12.139
What the hell is it this time?

48:12.223 --> 48:14.475
Sir, may I take a look at your foot?

48:14.558 --> 48:17.770
-Why would you look at my foot?
-We just need to check really quickly.

48:17.853 --> 48:20.189
Come over here if you've got a death wish.

48:20.272 --> 48:22.024
-[Hari gasps]
-[thunderclap]

48:22.108 --> 48:23.234
Ms. Yuk.

48:23.317 --> 48:25.277
I'm okay. Hurry and take a look at him.

48:27.196 --> 48:29.657
-Let me see your foot.
-What do you think you're doing?

48:29.740 --> 48:31.492
Let go. I said let go of me!

48:31.575 --> 48:32.618
I'm sorry. One second!

48:38.124 --> 48:39.959
[exhales sharply]

48:40.042 --> 48:42.670
-You knew you were diabetic, didn't you?
-Diabetic, my ass!

48:42.753 --> 48:44.171
It's just a little bruise!

48:44.255 --> 48:45.339
Bruise?

48:46.090 --> 48:47.883
I'm a plastic surgeon,

48:47.967 --> 48:50.428
and I've amputated dozens of toes
during my residency.

48:50.511 --> 48:52.847
You think I can't tell a bruised foot
from a diabetic one?

48:52.930 --> 48:54.473
So what? What do you want me to do?

48:54.557 --> 48:56.934
You have to go to a hospital right now!

48:59.228 --> 49:01.439
If you don't treat this,
you could lose your leg,

49:01.522 --> 49:03.607
and worst case, you could die of sepsis!

49:04.442 --> 49:06.026
-I don't care.
-Sir!

49:06.110 --> 49:08.487
This is my problem,
and I'll handle it myself!

49:09.405 --> 49:10.489
So please,

49:10.573 --> 49:12.741
don't tell my daughter about this,

49:13.617 --> 49:15.453
and pretend you didn't see anything.
STYLE
::cue()

49:16.162 --> 49:17.746
I'm begging you!

49:21.542 --> 49:22.626
No.

49:26.755 --> 49:28.424
I don't think I can do that.

49:54.200 --> 49:57.369
Looks like we'll have to
tell his daughter, right?

50:02.500 --> 50:03.501
Ms. Yuk?

50:06.003 --> 50:07.463
Dr. Do, just a moment.

50:09.048 --> 50:10.132
Please wait here.

50:10.799 --> 50:11.800
What?

50:13.093 --> 50:14.345
Ms. Yuk!

50:15.804 --> 50:16.931
Oh…

51:08.691 --> 51:12.152
PUBLIC HEALTH CENTER

51:27.418 --> 51:28.752
Dr. Do.

51:28.836 --> 51:29.837
Yes?

51:32.923 --> 51:35.718
Aren't you hungry?
Do you want to have some ramyeon?

51:35.801 --> 51:37.803
[♪ upbeat pop song plays]

51:40.347 --> 51:41.765
-Ramyeon?
-Yeah.

51:42.808 --> 51:43.809
[sniffles]

51:47.938 --> 51:48.939
-Well…
-[sniffles]

52:06.290 --> 52:08.292
[song continues]

52:17.801 --> 52:20.554
Why'd you make it
when I'm the one who suggested it?

52:22.222 --> 52:23.891
This was me repaying my debt.

52:23.974 --> 52:24.975
-Your debt?
-Yeah.

52:26.644 --> 52:27.645
You mean the spider?

52:29.229 --> 52:30.522
Oh, come on.

52:30.606 --> 52:35.027
I saved your life from a venomous spider,
and you want to call it even with this?

52:35.110 --> 52:37.154
No way. I'll get something bigger later.

52:37.237 --> 52:39.156
I already made it for you, okay?

52:39.239 --> 52:40.240
[chuckles]

52:44.161 --> 52:46.205
[knocks on door]

52:47.873 --> 52:49.124
Are we expecting someone?

52:50.292 --> 52:51.293
[Hari gasps]

52:52.336 --> 52:54.129
BREAK ROOM

53:06.016 --> 53:08.727
[thunderclap]

53:13.482 --> 53:14.525
Help me.

53:16.193 --> 53:17.236
Please…

53:18.112 --> 53:19.571
Help me live.

53:22.116 --> 53:24.410
[thunderclap]
STYLE
::cue()

53:32.626 --> 53:34.044
-[Jiui grunts]
-[Hari gasps]

53:36.422 --> 53:37.423
[groans]

53:41.051 --> 53:42.386
How does it look?

53:44.847 --> 53:47.391
The redness is widespread,
and judging by the fluctuance,

53:47.474 --> 53:49.643
it looks like a late-stage abscess.

53:52.896 --> 53:53.897
Let's perform an I&amp;D.

53:53.981 --> 53:55.607
Right. I'll make the preparations.

54:00.320 --> 54:01.447
[sighs]

54:16.712 --> 54:17.755
[Jeongbae] Doctor…

54:20.174 --> 54:22.259
Will I really make it out of this alive?

54:24.303 --> 54:25.471
Of course, sir.

54:26.764 --> 54:27.765
[sighs]

54:30.184 --> 54:31.185
[sighs]

55:22.194 --> 55:24.279
-I'll bring the antibiotics.
-[Jiui] Okay.

55:39.253 --> 55:41.088
Why did you change your mind?

55:47.469 --> 55:50.806
She told me not to feel guilty
for being alive.

55:54.017 --> 55:57.020
She said that would cause
too much pain to those left behind.

55:58.564 --> 56:00.190
That's what that nurse said.

56:02.901 --> 56:05.612
I'm just going to
keep living like this until I die,

56:05.696 --> 56:08.240
so stop harassing me and get lost!

56:13.078 --> 56:16.164
What about the family you leave behind
if you die like this?

56:17.666 --> 56:20.586
Do you think your family
will be able to just go on living?

56:21.962 --> 56:24.381
How do you expect your family
to go on living

56:25.591 --> 56:28.760
if you leave them no chance
to do anything about it?

56:33.473 --> 56:34.766
So, please…

56:38.895 --> 56:41.189
Please do it for your daughter, sir.

56:43.817 --> 56:44.818
Okay?

56:49.573 --> 56:53.493
[Jeongbae] What she said
brought me to my senses.

56:55.495 --> 56:57.372
When my wife was sick,

56:58.373 --> 57:03.503
that was the one thing
I struggled with the most.

57:05.881 --> 57:09.760
Seeing my wife
consumed by guilt for being alive.

57:12.137 --> 57:13.555
But I…

57:16.308 --> 57:22.356
[sobbing] …have been doing the same thing
to my daughter.

57:27.861 --> 57:30.530
[Jeongbae sobbing, sniffles]
STYLE
::cue()

57:42.125 --> 57:43.251
[sighs]

57:54.846 --> 57:57.015
He seems to have fallen asleep.
What do we do now?

57:58.684 --> 58:00.602
[Jiui] He had a lot of pus in him,

58:01.311 --> 58:03.980
so I think we should
monitor him here a little longer.

58:04.981 --> 58:06.733
Shall we let him sleep for a while?

58:07.901 --> 58:08.902
Yes.

58:14.700 --> 58:15.867
[Hari sighs]

58:23.041 --> 58:24.251
[Hari sighs]

58:24.960 --> 58:27.879
I thought things would be easier
at a public health center,

58:29.297 --> 58:31.842
but I had it better at an ER. [chuckles]

58:33.427 --> 58:34.678
[inhales sharply]

58:35.512 --> 58:36.555
Mmm…

58:38.348 --> 58:42.310
By the way, how did you know
that Mr. Kim Jeongbae was a diabetic?

58:44.229 --> 58:45.230
[inhales sharply]

58:45.313 --> 58:46.314
You said it yourself.

58:47.858 --> 58:52.195
That the easiest way
to hide a secret is to lash out.

58:54.114 --> 58:57.075
[inhales sharply]
For suffering patients with secrets,

58:57.159 --> 58:58.910
the answer is always treatment.

59:00.954 --> 59:01.955
Oh…

59:07.252 --> 59:10.088
-By the way, are you okay?
-Hmm?

59:11.173 --> 59:13.925
Ah… It's fine.
I'm sure it'll heal in no time.

59:14.009 --> 59:15.051
Stay right here.

59:16.303 --> 59:18.096
It's fine. I'm okay.

59:18.180 --> 59:19.514
Just sit back down.

59:19.598 --> 59:22.976
Why leave it like that?
We have medicine and a doctor to help you.

59:23.059 --> 59:24.311
Wait here.

59:24.394 --> 59:25.771
[stammers]

59:25.854 --> 59:27.689
I'm really fine, though…

59:34.654 --> 59:35.655
[softly] Let's see.

59:39.075 --> 59:40.243
Man, that must have stung.

59:47.083 --> 59:49.461
[♪ romantic ballad playing]

59:56.885 --> 59:57.886
Dr. Do.

01:00:02.974 --> 01:00:07.729
You said treatment was the answer
to a suffering patient's secrets, right?

01:00:08.605 --> 01:00:09.606
I did.

01:00:15.612 --> 01:00:17.239
Then what's your secret?

01:00:20.909 --> 01:00:21.952
What?

01:00:22.786 --> 01:00:24.287
You're also hurting.

01:00:25.413 --> 01:00:28.750
Every time you have to get on a boat,
you get so anxious you need medication.

01:00:28.834 --> 01:00:31.002
And you get mad
when people try to help you.

01:00:33.380 --> 01:00:35.465
Like someone who wants to hide something.

01:00:49.187 --> 01:00:50.856
I'm not crossing a line here.

01:00:52.691 --> 01:00:54.651
I'm asking as a nurse.

01:00:57.904 --> 01:01:00.657
Just like you want to treat me
because you're a doctor…

01:01:02.909 --> 01:01:04.369
I'm a nurse…

01:01:06.705 --> 01:01:09.040
so I want to help you,
since you're suffering.

01:01:10.125 --> 01:01:11.126
Okay?

01:01:15.922 --> 01:01:16.923
[sighs]

01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:24.055
Don't tell me if you don't want to.

01:01:24.139 --> 01:01:26.266
I can just find out myself. [chuckles]

01:01:28.393 --> 01:01:30.270
[song continues]
STYLE
::cue()

01:01:46.995 --> 01:01:48.079
[breathes shakily]

01:01:51.333 --> 01:01:52.334
[sighs]

01:01:53.126 --> 01:01:56.963
[ship horn blows]

01:01:58.632 --> 01:02:02.135
When you arrive on the mainland,
your daughter will be waiting for you.

01:02:03.553 --> 01:02:05.597
-I'm sorry about everything.
-[Hari chuckles]

01:02:05.680 --> 01:02:07.182
Don't worry about it. [chuckles]

01:02:07.265 --> 01:02:08.767
Good luck with your treatment.

01:02:08.850 --> 01:02:10.101
We'll be waiting for you.

01:02:18.068 --> 01:02:19.194
Thank you.

01:02:20.320 --> 01:02:23.323
[♪ heartfelt music plays]

01:02:26.409 --> 01:02:28.495
Thanks for giving me the courage.

01:02:37.629 --> 01:02:38.713
[sighs]

01:02:46.304 --> 01:02:47.389
Shall we go?

01:02:49.224 --> 01:02:50.225
Yes.

01:02:59.359 --> 01:03:02.946
[ship horn blows]

01:03:03.530 --> 01:03:05.991
-About Mr. Kim Jeongbae…
-Oh?

01:03:06.908 --> 01:03:09.786
Maybe we should have given him
some meds for seasickness.

01:03:10.328 --> 01:03:11.329
Huh?

01:03:12.831 --> 01:03:14.791
Well, getting seasick wouldn't be good.

01:03:15.959 --> 01:03:18.086
He works on a boat for a living, remember?

01:03:20.005 --> 01:03:21.756
-Oh…
-[chuckles]

01:03:21.840 --> 01:03:23.258
-Yes.
-You're right.

01:03:23.341 --> 01:03:27.012
PYEONDONGDO FISHING

01:03:36.396 --> 01:03:38.440
Hello, Mr. Park!

01:03:38.523 --> 01:03:39.983
-[Jiui] Mr. Park.
-Have you been somewhere?

01:03:40.066 --> 01:03:41.609
[Jiui] Are you feeling better?

01:03:46.614 --> 01:03:49.617
[♪ upbeat music plays]

01:03:54.581 --> 01:03:56.124
You lying bastard!

01:03:56.207 --> 01:03:57.417
[gasps]

01:04:21.441 --> 01:04:24.194
FOR SUFFERING PATIENTS
WITH SECRETS,

01:04:24.277 --> 01:04:29.282
THE ANSWER IS ALWAYS TREATMENT

01:04:48.885 --> 01:04:52.305
A LITTLE JOKING AROUND ON SET
REALLY BRINGS THE PLACE TO LIFE

01:05:00.396 --> 01:05:03.316
DOCTOR ON THE EDGE

01:05:03.399 --> 01:05:05.610
[stammers] Mr. Park, what brings you here?

01:05:05.693 --> 01:05:08.071
-[shouts]
-[Mr. Park] You lying quack!

01:05:08.154 --> 01:05:10.406
Is he seriously trying to ruin my life?

01:05:11.199 --> 01:05:12.617
-[exclaims]
-[Jiui] Hey, Lee Jangsu!

01:05:13.368 --> 01:05:15.078
What did I do wrong just now?

01:05:15.161 --> 01:05:16.329
[screams]

01:05:16.412 --> 01:05:17.455
[Hari] Were you waiting for me?

01:05:17.539 --> 01:05:20.041
We have plenty of time to spare.
Would you like a drink?

01:05:20.125 --> 01:05:21.918
Was that so hard?

01:05:22.001 --> 01:05:24.921
[Jucheon] It's like something out of
a late '80s movie.

01:05:25.004 --> 01:05:27.215
[Hari] Doctor, come with me.

01:05:27.298 --> 01:05:29.717
[Hyeon] Are we really going to sleep
in the same room?

01:05:29.801 --> 01:05:31.010
[Hari] Do you regret it?

01:05:32.846 --> 01:05:34.848
Translated by Yoon Hyuk Park
